hint.chicken=Wild chickens drift toward a coop with a full trough, a bit of hay and somewhere dusty to scratch.
hint.chicken.rare=Folk say a golden hen only stops where flowers grow and the trough is heaped with her favourite corn.
hint.cow=A cow wanders in when there is grass to graze, hay to spare and plenty of open room.
hint.cow.rare=A red highland cow is drawn to a well-kept barn with hay, where at least two cows are truly content.
hint.pig=Pigs follow their noses to food, a muddy wallow, water and a few vegetables.
hint.pig.rare=A spotted pig is rumoured to sniff out a sty with mud and a little hoard of truffles waiting in it.
hint.sheep=Sheep come grazing where the grass is good, the flowers bloom and the land is open.
hint.sheep.rare=A black sheep only lingers by a fold with grass and flowers that is close to perfect in every way.
hint.frog=Frogs hop over to fresh water with lily pads, reeds and a little shade.
hint.frog.rare=A purple frog has been seen at ponds with lily pads and reeds, where a few frogs already live happily.
